    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's actually a really good start. It feels professional and the keywords are woven in quite naturally. \n\nThe problem is, our internal tester just ran a simulation on a similar draft and the \"Term Coverage\" score was still only around 70% because it missed a few nuances. We really need to push that score as close to 1.0 as possible to ensure they pass the first filter.\n\nCan you try another version? Try to get every single one of those terms in there—if you miss even one, the score drops significantly. Just please, I'm begging you, don't make it look like a list. If I see a sentence that's just \"I have experience in X, Y, and Z,\" the recruiter will reject it immediately. Keep it sounding like a real human being wrote it, but hit every single keyword on that list. \n\nCan you get us to a 1.0 score while keeping that premium tone?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
